  "question": {
    "text": "A triangle is formed by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-axis, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math>-axis and the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></math>. Then the number of points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;which lie strictly inside the triangle, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;is an integer and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> is a multiple of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>, is _____ ."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "31",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>20</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0072_87405fb53312.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 256px;\" /></p><p>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>57</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p><p>So, points are</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>14</mn></math>&nbsp;points.</p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>27</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>So, points are</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;points.</p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>51</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn></math></p><p>So, points are</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;points.</p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p><p>So, points are</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;points.</p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>45</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p><p>So, points are</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;points.</p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>So, point is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;point</p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>39</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn></math></p><p>So, point&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;point</p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p>So, point is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;point</p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>33</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> no point</p><p>Total points inside the triangle</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>31</mn></math>&nbsp;points</p>"
  }
